WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.122
Week 17: Preterite: Completed Events. report what happened sequence completed actions ask follow-up questions

2
00:00:08.122 --> 00:00:21.303
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can report what happened, sequence completed actions, ask follow-up questions. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:21.303 --> 00:00:28.358
Language system. Regular preterite; spelling changes; time markers; completed event chains.

4
00:00:28.358 --> 00:00:35.947
Sound and delivery. Preterite stress contrasts such as hablo/habló and trabajo/trabajó.

5
00:00:35.947 --> 00:00:45.479
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:45.479 --> 00:01:09.689
Model language. Ayer llegué temprano a la oficina. — Yesterday I arrived early at the office. Primero revisamos el informe. — First we reviewed the report. Luego llamaron al supervisor. — Then they called the supervisor. ¿Qué ocurrió después? — What happened afterward? La reunión terminó a las seis. — The meeting finished at six.

7
00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:19.694
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
